## Multi-Agent Workflow

Development uses seven roles — Controller, Planner, Coder, Runner, Reviewer,
Author, Researcher — assigned by the user at chat start ("you are the
planner agent"). If told to "run the coder and runner in this session," act
as Controller and spawn the roles as subagents (spawn titles `role(model):
task`, e.g. `coder(<mid-tier model>): <task>`; utility spawns keep plain
titles).

**CRITICAL:** `harness/harness.md` holds the loop and the shared rules every
role must follow; `harness/roles/<role>.md` holds your role's namespace,
tier, constraints, and handoff protocol. Read the core plus your own role
file — not the other roles' files. Rule detail docs under `harness/rules/`
are read only when a rule's trigger matches your next action.

## Command Execution & Approval Policy

Command execution is programmatically guarded by `.agents/hooks.json` via
`.agents/hooks/command_guard.py` before `run_command` executes:

- **Auto-allowed (`allow`)**: `[SET AT SETUP: PACKAGE_MANAGER_SYNC_CMD]`,
  `[SET AT SETUP: PACKAGE_MANAGER_RUN_CMD]`, `[SET AT SETUP: TEST_CMD]`,
<!-- SECTION:latex_on:start -->
  `latexmk`/`bibtex`/`pdflatex`/`xelatex`/`lualatex`,
<!-- SECTION:latex_on:end -->
  read-only git queries
  (`git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git show`, `git branch`),
  and non-destructive inspections (`ls`, `cat`, `grep`, `rg`, `find`, `pwd`).
- **Requires user approval (`force_ask`)**: State-modifying git commands (`git commit`,
  `git push`, `git checkout`, `git switch`, `git reset`), background jobs (`systemd-run`,
  `setsid`), dependency modifications (`[SET AT SETUP: PACKAGE_MANAGER_ADD_CMD]` and its
  remove counterpart), file deletions (`rm`, `unlink`), and unclassified commands.
- **Strictly forbidden (`deny`)**: Privilege escalation (`sudo`, `su`), force pushes (`git push --force`),
  destructive wipes (`rm -rf /`), and piping remote web scripts to shell (`curl | sh`).

